# ============================================================================
# Binary Paths (Required for Docker Runtime)
# ============================================================================
# Terraform binary path (must be executable and match container architecture)
# Note: Terraform CLI is currently in beta. Contact your HashiCorp representative to obtain the binary.
# Example for macOS ARM64: /opt/homebrew/bin/terraform
# Example for Linux AMD64: /usr/local/bin/terraform
TERRAFORM_BINARY_PATH=/path/to/terraform

# tfpolicy binary path (must be executable and match container architecture)
# Note: tfpolicy is currently in beta. Contact your HashiCorp representative to obtain the binary.
TFPOLICY_BINARY_PATH=/path/to/tfpolicy

# MCP Server Configuration (already set in Dockerfile, no need to change)
POLICY_DB=database/policy_spec_db.jsonl
POLICY_SUMMARY=database/POLICY_SUMMARY.md

# ============================================================================
# Execution Mode: OpenCode
# ============================================================================

# --- OpenCode Mode ---
# OpenCode supports multiple authentication providers
# IMPORTANT: Choose ONE authentication provider below. Do NOT uncomment both sections.

# --- OpenCode with LiteLLM (Default) ---
# AUTH_PROVIDER=litellm
# MODEL_BASE_URL=https://your-litellm-endpoint.com
# MODEL_NAME=aws/claude-sonnet-4-5
# MODEL_API_KEY=sk-your-litellm-api-key

# --- OpenCode with GitHub Copilot ---
# AUTH_PROVIDER=github-copilot
# MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet-4.6
# GITHUB_COPILOT_ACCESS_TOKEN=gho_your_access_token
# GITHUB_COPILOT_REFRESH_TOKEN=gho_your_refresh_token  # Optional, defaults to access token
# GITHUB_COPILOT_EXPIRES=0  # Optional, defaults to 0
#
# Please chose models supported by GitHub Copilot such as:
#   - claude-sonnet-4.6
#   - gpt-5.2
# Note: claude-sonnet-4.5 is not supported by GitHub Copilot (verified as of June 2026)
#
# Note: You can find your GitHub Copilot tokens in:
# ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json (on your host machine)
# The container will automatically create auth.json from these environment variables

# --- OpenCode with Amazon Bedrock (Bearer Token) ---
# AUTH_PROVIDER=amazon-bedrock
# MODEL_NAME=anthropic.claude-opus-4-5-20251101-v1:0
# MODEL_API_KEY=your-base64-encoded-bedrock-bearer-token

# ============================================================================
# External Repository Path (Primary use case)
# ============================================================================
# Path to external repository containing Sentinel policies
# Set this to automatically extract and convert Sentinel policies from an external repository
# Can be absolute or relative path
#
# Examples:
#   EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR=/Users/xxx/git/company/sentinel-policies
#   EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR=../../workdir/workspaces/external_repo
#   EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR=/absolute/path/to/sentinel/repo
#
# When EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR is set:
#   - run.sh automatically uses external mode
#   - Sentinel files are extracted from this directory
#   - Generated policies are deployed to EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR/tfpolicy/
#   - Timestamped input/output directories are created automatically
#
# When EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR is NOT set:
#   - run.sh uses local mode
#   - You need to prepare input files manually in DATA_DIR/INPUT_DIR/
EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR=/path/to/your/sentinel-repository

# Path to sentinel.hcl file (Optional)
# If specified, the file will be copied and processed during preprocessing
# Examples:
#   SENTINEL_HCL_PATH=/path/to/sentinel.hcl
#   SENTINEL_HCL_PATH=./external_repo/sentinel.hcl
# SENTINEL_HCL_PATH=

# ============================================================================
# Pipeline Configuration (for local mode)
# ============================================================================
# These settings are used when EXTERNAL_REPO_DIR is not set
# Data directory for input/output files (mounted to container's /workspace/data)
# Relative paths are resolved from current working directory (where you run the command)
#
# Examples:
#   DATA_DIR=./data                           # Recommended: Create data/ in your working directory
#   DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data           # Use absolute path for clarity
#   DATA_DIR=../shared-data                   # Relative to current working directory
#
# Note for developers:
#   If running from repository root, use: DATA_DIR=terraform-pac-agent/data
DATA_DIR=./data

# Input subdirectory within DATA_DIR (host-side directory name)
# This directory is mounted to container's /workspace/data/input
# Examples:
#   INPUT_DIR=input           # Default: data/input/ -> /workspace/data/input
#   INPUT_DIR=input2          # Alternative: data/input2/ -> /workspace/data/input
INPUT_DIR=input

# Output subdirectory within DATA_DIR (host-side directory name)
# This directory is mounted to container with the same name
# Multiple output directories can coexist without interfering with each other
# For full pipeline runs and step0-extraction, existing non-empty OUTPUT_DIR is rejected
# to prevent accidental overwrite. Set a new OUTPUT_DIR in .env for each new run.
#
# NOTE: When using external mode, OUTPUT_DIR is automatically generated
# with a timestamp (e.g., output-20260603_012345) and this setting is ignored.
# This prevents conflicts when processing multiple batches from external repositories.
#
# Examples:
#   OUTPUT_DIR=output           # Default: data/output/ -> /workspace/data/output
#   OUTPUT_DIR=output-v2        # Experiment: data/output-v2/ -> /workspace/data/output-v2
#   OUTPUT_DIR=results-20260521 # Timestamped: data/results-20260521/ -> /workspace/data/results-20260521
OUTPUT_DIR=output

# Input file for policy extraction (Step 0)
# Relative to DATA_DIR/INPUT_DIR/ directory
# Examples:
#   INPUT_FILE=policy_goal.txt         # Default: DATA_DIR/INPUT_DIR/policy_goal.txt
#   INPUT_FILE=custom_goals.txt        # Custom input file
INPUT_FILE=policy_goal.txt

# Maximum number of parallel workers for pipeline execution
MAX_WORKERS=5  # Optional, defaults to 5 if not set

# Docker image configuration
IMAGE_NAME=icr.io/terraform-policy-agent-2026/terraform-pac-agent  # Optional, defaults to terraform-pac-agent-skills
IMAGE_TAG=0.0.31  # Optional, defaults to latest

# Container name prefix for Docker containers
# Useful for running multiple environments (dev/staging/prod) or multiple users on the same host
# Examples:
#   CONTAINER_PREFIX=terraform-pac-agent-skills  # Default
#   CONTAINER_PREFIX=dev-pac                     # Development environment
#   CONTAINER_PREFIX=staging-pac                 # Staging environment
#   CONTAINER_PREFIX=user1-pac                   # Multi-user setup
CONTAINER_PREFIX=terraform-pac-agent-skills  # Optional, defaults to terraform-pac-agent-skills

# ============================================================================
# Container CLI Configuration
# ============================================================================
# Container CLI used to build and run the agent: docker or podman
# Priority: this .env file > environment variable > default (docker)
# Examples:
#   DOCKER_CLI=docker    Default
#   DOCKER_CLI=podman    Use Podman instead of Docker
#
# NOTE: Do not append an inline "#" comment to the line below. The value is
# read verbatim by pre_check.py, so a trailing comment becomes part of it.
DOCKER_CLI=docker

# Extra arguments appended to the container run command (optional)
# Use this for host-specific flags that the agent cannot detect on its own.
#
# IMPORTANT: Wrap the value in double quotes whenever it contains a space.
# Without quotes the shell reads only the first word.
#
# SELinux hosts (RHEL / Fedora / CentOS Stream):
#   Podman on an SELinux-enforcing host denies the bind mounts unless the
#   container is permitted to read them. Prefer label=disable over adding ",z"
#   to the mounts: ",z" relabels the files on the host and would therefore
#   modify the labels of shared binaries such as /usr/local/bin/terraform.
#     DOCKER_RUN_EXTRA_ARGS="--security-opt label=disable"
#
# Rootless Podman on Linux (host.docker.internal is not resolvable):
#     DOCKER_RUN_EXTRA_ARGS=--add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway
#
# Both of the above at once (SELinux-enforcing Linux host):
#     DOCKER_RUN_EXTRA_ARGS="--security-opt label=disable --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway"
#
# Do NOT set --add-host on macOS (Podman Desktop / podman machine): the VM already
# defines host.docker.internal, and Podman fails with
# 'unable to replace "host-gateway" of host entry "host.docker.internal"'.
#
# DOCKER_RUN_EXTRA_ARGS=

# ============================================================================
# Timeout Configuration (in seconds)
# ============================================================================
# Stage 0: Policy Extraction timeout
STAGE0_TIMEOUT=600  # Optional, defaults to 600 (10 minutes)

# Stage 1: Requirement Generation timeout (per goal)
STAGE1_TIMEOUT=300  # Optional, defaults to 300 (5 minutes)

# Stage 2: Policy Generation timeout (per policy)
STAGE2_TIMEOUT=900  # Optional, defaults to 900 (15 minutes)
# Note: For complex policies, consider increasing to 900 or more (15 minutes)

# Stage 4: Validation Fixtures Generation (Optional)
# Enable/disable Stage 4 (validation fixtures generation)
ENABLE_STAGE4=false  # Optional, defaults to false. Set to true to enable
# Stage 4: Validation Fixtures Generation timeout (per policy)
STAGE4_TIMEOUT=300  # Optional, defaults to 300 (5 minutes)

# Stage 3: Summary Generation timeout
# Total timeout = STAGE3_TIMEOUT_BASE + (policy_count * STAGE3_TIMEOUT_PER_POLICY)
STAGE3_TIMEOUT_BASE=180  # Optional, defaults to 180 (3 minutes base)
STAGE3_TIMEOUT_PER_POLICY=60  # Optional, defaults to 60 (1 minute per policy)

# ============================================================================
# Retry Configuration
# ============================================================================
# Maximum number of retries for failed tasks
# When a task fails (timeout, error, etc.), it will be retried up to MAX_RETRIES times
# Note: Retry timeout is automatically increased by 1.5x for each retry attempt
# Examples:
#   MAX_RETRIES=1  # Default: Retry once (total 2 attempts: initial + 1 retry)
#   MAX_RETRIES=0  # No retries (only initial attempt)
#   MAX_RETRIES=3  # Retry up to 3 times (total 4 attempts)
MAX_RETRIES=1  # Optional, defaults to 1 (backward compatible)
